<article class="env-proposition" id="29AB">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/29AB">Proposition <span data-tag="29AB">5.2.4.2</span>.</a> Let $F: \calC \rightarrow \calD $ be a functor between $\infty $-categories. The following are equivalent: </p>
  <p><ul>
  <li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(1)$"><p>
The functor $F$ has a right adjoint. 
</p>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(2)$"><p>
For every pullback diagram 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix { \overline{\calC } \ar [r] \ar [d]^{p'} &  \overline{\calD } \ar [d]^{p} \\ \calC \ar [r]^{F} &  \calD , } \]
</div>
<p>
 if $p$ is a representable right fibration, then $p'$ is also a representable right fibration. 
</p>
</li>
</ul></p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $\calM $ be a correspondence from $\calC $ to $\calD $ associated to $F$, and apply Lemma <a href="/tag/C625" data-tag="C625">5.2.4.1</a> to each object of $D$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>